  "user_id": 18603,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Ad Transparency Lab\r\n\r\nUse the CHAT Framework to create a simple filter and sorting algorithm to help serve targeted ads to users of a popular social media site.\r\n\r\n### 1. Clarify\r\n* Inspect the data in the code, and decompose ways that you might filter and sort this data.\r\n* Decide what your algorithm values most.\r\n\r\n### 2. Hone / Apply (Build the Filter)\r\n* Determine how you want to filter this data \r\n* Work with AI Tutor to implement a filtering function.\r\n\r\n### 3. Hone / Apply (Build the Sorter)\r\n* Sort the data that remains by an algorithm of your design.\r\n* Work with AI Tutor to implement a sorting function.\r\n\r\n### 4. Hone / Apply (Create the Pipeline)\r\n* Connect the pipeline at the bottom: sort > filter > render\r\n* Ask AI Tutor to generate test cases in order to check for proper implementation and inclusiveness.\r\n\r\n### 5. Transfer\r\n* Create a generalizable system prompt that will create a basic *filter > sort > render* pipeline. Save it into your backpack.\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
